 | SCENARIO-VERIFY-5323 | Native Backend Bisect Opens Or Blocks Runtime Candidate | Implemented | Artifact follows the complete native-runtime path with `runtime_unblocked_min_one_mandated=true`, `sota_backend_candidate_ready=true`, `timeout_or_crash_root_cause.value=none`, and a `flagship_dense` `llama-cli` receipt completing load, first token, and bounded 8-token generation with authenticated offload. The best attempt records context=512, batch=512, ubatch=128, n_predict=8, first_token_latency_s=19.374111400917172, generated_token_count=8, gpu_memory_delta_mb=18630, returncode=0, and timeout_class=completed_no_timeout; llama-completion and llama-server were skipped after the candidate was found. The artifact also records `flagged_adversarial=true` with pending `DURATION_TOO_SHORT` critical and `METHODOLOGY_MISSING` warn corrigenda. Focused pytest, focused 100% new-module coverage, and ruff passed per artifact; repo-wide spec coverage and tests/python retained pre-existing failures/interruption. No retro closure, AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement, violation_rate, SOTA quality, answer accuracy, or hardware speedup claim is recorded. |
 | REQ-VERIFY-5324 | Local Native GGUF Runtime Receipt Stabilization V486 | Implemented | `python/carnot/experiment_5324_runtime_receipt_stabilization_v486.py`; `tests/python/test_experiment_5324_runtime_receipt_stabilization_v486.py`; `openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md`; `results/experiment_5324_runtime_receipt_stabilization_v486.json`; honest_verdict={"principle":"Terminal verdict must start with complete: or blocked_ and state whether the native SOTA runtime receipt is repeatably stable.","value":"complete: local_native_llama_cpp_stability_receipts=flagship_dense:llama-cli"}; status.value=complete; sota_runtime_unblocked_stable=true; repeated_receipts completed=3/3 with generated_token_count=8 each; first_token_latency_s=[37.60843323683366,17.155047603184357,17.1296031170059]; gpu_memory_delta_mb=18630 each; quality_claim_permitted=false; no retro_* flags; no AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement/violation_rate fields; no SOTA quality, answer accuracy, or hardware speedup claim is made. |
 | SCENARIO-VERIFY-5324 | Exp5323 Candidate Replays Into Stable Or Blocked Receipts | Implemented | Artifact follows the complete native-runtime stability path by replaying the Exp5323 `flagship_dense` `llama-cli` candidate three times with context=512, batch=512, ubatch=128, n_predict=8, timeout_s=240.0, and authenticated offload. All 3 receipts completed load, first token, and bounded 8-token generation without timeout, with max GPU memory delta 18630 MB each. Focused pytest passed with addopts disabled and focused new-module coverage passed at 100%; the repo global coverage gate retained a pre-existing python/carnot tree failure. No retro closure, AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement, violation_rate, SOTA quality, answer accuracy, or hardware speedup claim is recorded. |
+| REQ-VERIFY-5325 | Theoria Deterministic Rewrite-State Fixture V486 | Implemented | `python/carnot/experiment_5325_theoria_rewrite_state_fixture_v486.py`; `tests/python/test_experiment_5325_theoria_rewrite_state_fixture_v486.py`; `openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md`; `data/rewrite_state_fixture_v486.json`; `results/experiment_5325_theoria_rewrite_state_fixture_v486.json`; honest_verdict={"principle":"Terminal verdict must start with complete: or blocked_ and state whether Exp5326 can consume the deterministic rewrite-state fixture.","value":"complete: deterministic rewrite-state fixture usable by Exp5326"}; status.value=complete; rewrite_state_fixture_ready=true; rewrite_case_count=6; complete_change_coverage_rate=1.0; rewrite_acceptability_rate=1.0; unsafe_rewrite_rejection_rate=1.0; false_accept_count=0; no retro_* flags; no AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement/violation_rate fields; no live-model quality or hardware-speedup claim is made. |
+| SCENARIO-VERIFY-5325 | Typed Rewrite Transitions Accept Safe Rewrites And Reject Unsafe Ones | Implemented | Artifact follows the deterministic rewrite-state fixture path across six case types: safe_paraphrase, contradiction_introduction, missing_required_change, fabricated_premise_citation, invalid_premise_preserved, and overbroad_rewrite. It records the safe paraphrase accepted, five unsafe or invalid rewrites rejected, complete_change_coverage_rate=1.0, rewrite_acceptability_rate=1.0, unsafe_rewrite_rejection_rate=1.0, false_accept_count=0, and consumer_contract.next_experiment=Exp5326. No retro closure, AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement, violation_rate, live LLM quality, or hardware speedup claim is recorded. |
